---
import { BookOpen } from 'lucide-react';
import Section from './Section.astro';
const year = 2026;
---

{/* Introduction */}
<Section
  id="intro"
  title="Introduction: The 'Bonus' Mirage"
  icon={BookOpen}
>
  <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
    Habari, traders. It's Patrick Mahinge here.
  </p>
  <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
    A new trader that I am mentoring recently asked me, <em
      >"Which forex broker gives the biggest deposit bonus?"</em
    > It's a natural question. When you're starting with limited capital, a 50% or
    100% boost feels like a lifeline.
  </p>
  <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
    But let's be honest with each other: <strong
      >Choosing a broker based only on a bonus is like choosing a marathon shoe
      based only on the color of its laces.</strong
    > It looks good at the start line, but it won't help you survive the 42 kilometers
    ahead.
  </p>
  <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
    In this {year} review, we are tackling the elephant in the room: <strong
      >Why does Pepperstone, a top-tier, CMA-regulated forex broker, not offer
      deposit bonuses in Kenya?</strong
    > Is this a weakness? Or is it actually the ultimate sign of respect for your
    capital? I've done the homework so you don't have to.
  </p>
</Section>
